Jahshaka patch 0028 — a reflection probe only reaches a material that can
reflect it.

WHY (owner, 2026-09-13, REFLECTION_PROBE_AUDIT.md Q1): "[reflection probes]
should only affect reflective objects in a scene." At this pin there is NO
material-side gate anywhere in the probe chain. `HlmsPbs::
notifyPropertiesMergedPreGenerationStep` sets `use_envprobe_map` and
`use_parallax_correct_cubemaps` for EVERY datablock as soon as the PASS property
`parallax_correct_cubemaps` is set, and the per-pixel probe loop
(`forwardPlusDoCubemaps`) is inserted from the PASS property
`hlms_enable_cubemaps_auto` — so a rough grey wall runs the same eight
readOnlyFetches, two localCorrects and cube-array sample per overlapping probe
that a chrome sphere does. The only conditional in the whole chain is
`pixelData.roughness < 1.0f || vctSpecular.w == 0`, which excludes a
perfectly-rough surface and only while VCT is live.

THE GATE IS THE MATERIAL'S OWN REFLECTANCE, not a roughness threshold — roughness
blurs a reflection, it never removes one. Unreal spells the same control as the
Specular input (default 0.5 = ~4% reflectance, 0 = reflects nothing) and likewise
has no per-material "receives reflections" tick.

WHY IT CANNOT CHANGE A PIXEL. The PBS specular environment term ends as

    Rs = envColourS * pixelData.specular * (F0 * envBRDF.x + envBRDF.y)

with `pixelData.specular = material.kS`
(Samples/Media/Hlms/Pbs/Any/Main/800.PixelShader_piece_ps.any:307). A datablock
whose SPECULAR COLOUR is black therefore multiplies every environment term by
zero, and skipping the lookup is arithmetically identical rather than an
approximation. The gate additionally requires no authored F0 (the second half of
the pair the owner named: F0 alone leaves the Schlick rim and the envBRDF bias),
which makes it a strict subset of that provably-zero case. A physically lit
dielectric has kS = 1 and never qualifies — it keeps its ~4% sheen.

TWO EXCLUSIONS, both because kS does not scale them:
  * clear coat — `clearCoatEnvColourS` is not multiplied by kS, so a
    zero-kS clear-coated material still reflects and keeps the loop;
  * `cubemaps_as_diffuse_gi` — there a probe also carries DIFFUSE light. Off in
    Jahshaka (`setAmbientLight(..., envFeatures = 0)`), checked anyway.

`needs_env_brdf` is untouched: it is also raised by `hlms_enable_cubemaps_auto`,
so the irradiance field's and VCT's diffuse still reach the surface.

WHAT IT TOUCHES
  * SOURCE  Components/Hlms/Pbs/include/OgreHlmsPbs.h  — one property id.
  * SOURCE  Components/Hlms/Pbs/src/OgreHlmsPbs.cpp    — the predicate in
    calculateHashForPreCreate, the gate in
    notifyPropertiesMergedPreGenerationStep.
  * MEDIA   Samples/Media/Hlms/Pbs/Any/Main/800.PixelShader_piece_ps.any —
    `@insertpiece( forwardPlusDoCubemaps )` becomes conditional on the
    DATABLOCK property `use_parallax_correct_cubemaps`. Without this hunk the
    C++ half saves nothing: the piece is defined from a pass property.

SOURCE patch (not media-only): every tree must re-run build-ogre.sh.
The media file is CRLF; edited in binary mode.

Covered by tests/gi/test_gi_probe_gate.cpp (gi.probe_gate).
